Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.62,0:00:21.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good luck with that, soldier.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.47,0:00:38.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can smell the Ishbalan stray dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.52,0:00:39.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.56,0:00:42.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he's gone now.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.40,0:00:46.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Say, Brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.07,0:00:49.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,what's going to happen to Marcoh-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.86,0:00:51.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer said he was going to look after him.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.07,0:00:55.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What can we do about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.21,0:01:08.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}The Central Library?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.67,0:01:14.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Marcoh-san had to hide all of his materials right under the military's nose.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.10,0:01:19.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And this...\N{\an8}What do you suppose that means?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.77,0:01:20.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.39,0:01:24.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In any case, let's keep this a secret from the Colonel and the others.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.65,0:01:25.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.73,0:01:28.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whether or not we can trust them anymore...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.03,0:01:31.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.07,0:01:36.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything\Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.83,0:01:41.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything,\Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.12,0:01:46.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's\NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.84,0:01:52.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that\Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.52,0:03:30.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're leaving so suddenly?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.40,0:03:31.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.32,0:03:33.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now that we know that Scar is in East City,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.03,0:03:37.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,everyone seems to have become\Nworried about Central all of a sudden.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.86,0:03:40.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry to have inconvenienced you,\Nbut we're going back.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.99,0:03:42.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Before you do,\Nwhat is your punishment?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.99,0:03:43.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Punishment?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.12,0:03:48.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I knew where the Crystal Alchemist was, \Nand yet I left him alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.08,0:03:52.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've done well.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.09,0:03:57.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wanted to place him in protective custody.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.80,0:04:01.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The officer directly underneath me—\NGrand—was against it,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.68,0:04:06.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but he put his research to use on the battlefield, which must have tormented him.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.68,0:04:09.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At this late date, I would like to make it up to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.31,0:04:13.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, concerning his research...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.27,0:04:14.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That will be all.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.61,0:04:16.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will continue to rely on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.03,0:04:22.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,May you have a safe journey.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.45,0:04:29.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stone...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.37,0:04:31.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,does not exist.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.75,0:04:36.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As you can see, I'm fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.63,0:04:44.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You'd probably shape up\Nif you did get punished once.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.76,0:04:47.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He never seems to\Nlet his guard down.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.44,0:04:53.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Creation follows destruction!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.15,0:04:58.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I shall fix you up nice and pretty!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.95,0:05:02.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Th-That's all right...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.49,0:05:05.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The method of bonding a soul to armor...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.03,0:05:08.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is only known by one person:
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.54,0:05:10.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fullmetal.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.87,0:05:16.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and for that to happen, I first \Nneed to do something about my arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.25,0:05:17.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.80,0:05:20.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all, if Edward-kun is unable to use his alchemy...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.88,0:05:23.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...he's just a sharp-tongued brat.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.39,0:05:29.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Anyhow, I'm going to my mechanic.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.77,0:05:31.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel, you know who, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.06,0:05:32.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.98,0:05:37.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I saw our good-for-nothing alchemist there once, bawling in pain.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.77,0:05:42.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"It hurts! It hurts so bad!\NI'm going to pee my pants!" Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.03,0:05:47.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you going to do once you're fixed up?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.45,0:05:50.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.08,0:05:53.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's something I want to look up in the library there.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.87,0:05:56.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's going to be a long trip.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.92,0:05:57.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Which means...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.25,0:06:01.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Since I'm part of the Führer's party, I won't be able to accompany you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.80,0:06:05.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't very well leave here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.68,0:06:07.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And I have to\Nkeep an eye on him.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.18,0:06:12.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't think I'd be able to protect\Nthose two from such a dangerous guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.77,0:06:14.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That goes for me too!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.15,0:06:16.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That settles it, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.94,0:06:21.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I shall escort these two during their journey!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.94,0:06:24.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We don't need that!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.40,0:06:27.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you going to do if Scar\Nattacks you again in your condition?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.49,0:06:32.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't carry Al\Nlike that either, can you?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.21,0:06:40.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Children should listen to adults.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.71,0:06:42.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Y-You're calling us children?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.55,0:06:43.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, say something!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.09,0:06:48.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother! This is the first time anyone has ever treated me like a child since I got this body!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.97,0:06:52.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Very well, Edward Elric...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.56,0:06:55.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shall we begin packing?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.57,0:07:11.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the first time anyone has ever\Ntreated me like luggage since I got this body.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.79,0:07:14.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For crying out loud...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.04,0:07:20.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, newspaper?\NI've got tea as well!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.38,0:07:21.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shoo, shoo!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.55,0:07:23.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, I've got a message from Roy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.55,0:07:24.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,From the Colonel?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.88,0:07:28.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Don't go dying under my command.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.43,0:07:29.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a pain having to deal with everything."\NThat is all.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.34,0:07:30.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tell him, "Roger.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.26,0:07:34.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no way I'm going to die ahead of you, you grubby colonel."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.60,0:07:38.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And while you're at it,\Ntake this escort with you, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.31,0:07:39.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, now...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.82,0:07:46.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know what Marcoh told you,\Nbut let me inform you of one thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.70,0:07:52.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Three years ago,\Nwe discovered the body of a young girl who had been transmuted into a Chimera.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.91,0:07:53.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nina?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.83,0:07:56.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The way she was torn apart...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.83,0:08:00.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It turns out to be identical to Scar's method of alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.34,0:08:09.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.01,0:08:13.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now I can take him on.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.93,0:08:18.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll see you in Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.39,0:08:20.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll apply for permission to browse at the first branch.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.77,0:08:23.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You'll have to excuse me for using my left hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.36,0:08:27.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Central...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.65,0:08:30.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Central's first... first something-or-other!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.61,0:08:32.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Central Library, First Branch.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.82,0:08:35.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.12,0:08:35.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's enough, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.04,0:08:40.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.50,0:08:42.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.93,0:09:00.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is the Führer...\NWhat is the Führer's answer?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.12,0:09:17.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You told that boy where your materials are hidden, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.66,0:09:19.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.62,0:09:21.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.41,0:09:23.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The boy will come even closer to the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.38,0:09:26.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, I would be a little upset
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.21,0:09:30.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,if you wrote down anything extra in those materials.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.67,0:09:32.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The boy is smart.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.68,0:09:36.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once he reads it, he won't do as you want him to.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.72,0:09:43.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Which is why, before he does,\NI thought I'd look into it myself, you see?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.23,0:09:45.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That won't be possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.69,0:09:48.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're going to die...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.69,0:09:49.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,right here!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.41,0:10:05.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was cruel.\NI've already died once, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.80,0:10:12.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So that's it!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.88,0:10:15.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just like the stories say,\Nyou guys are...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.76,0:10:17.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gluttony...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.89,0:10:22.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tell me...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.10,0:10:27.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Where did you tell the boy you hid your materials?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.11,0:10:34.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whew, I've had it, Al.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.28,0:10:37.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That guy just keeps\Ngoing on and on,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.07,0:10:41.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and all he does is brag about his family background.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.24,0:10:43.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let me take a break here—
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.71,0:10:45.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.04,0:10:50.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al? {\alpha&HFF&}Al? Al? Al? Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.13,0:10:51.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.21,0:10:56.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al got mistaken for someone else's luggage and was dropped off at the last station!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.72,0:10:59.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hm? That won't do. We'll go back for him at the next station.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.80,0:11:00.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't wait that long!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.14,0:11:02.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now, now...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.31,0:11:04.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stay out of my way!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.81,0:11:07.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Calm down, Edward Elric.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.94,0:11:11.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What else could I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.57,0:11:17.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I, a suit of armor, said "not here," they would just be stunned by me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.78,0:11:21.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder if Brother has noticed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.12,0:11:27.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm{\i0} the one who wants to cry, here!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.12,0:11:28.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh-oh...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.10,0:11:49.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He wouldn't have gone off somewhere by himself!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.19,0:11:51.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're sure...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.52,0:11:53.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it was this armor?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.07,0:11:56.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.\NYou're good at drawing, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.78,0:11:59.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a technique for drawing likenesses that has been passed down in my family for generations.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.86,0:12:01.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can you be\Ntaking this so lightly?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.03,0:12:03.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait, it's too dangerous!\NWhat's the hurry?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.24,0:12:07.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You guys just don't understand us!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.33,0:12:08.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.37,0:12:10.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard from Doctor Marcoh!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.25,0:12:12.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,About what happened in Ishbal!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.24,0:12:46.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Say, do you know anything about some armor that was at the train station?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.49,0:12:47.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Like who might've taken it?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.91,0:12:50.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was large and dark...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.96,0:12:53.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just a second, please!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.81,0:13:07.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ee-yow...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.27,0:13:17.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey! Hold it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.28,0:13:25.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on!\NHold on, I tell you!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.87,0:13:30.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Damn.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.46,0:13:33.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I had my arm and leg, this wouldn't be so hard...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.56,0:14:00.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is trouble... We're getting farther\Nand farther away from the train station.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.65,0:14:04.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ahem...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.53,0:14:06.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Am I hearing things?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.03,0:14:09.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm right here. This armor.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.63,0:14:20.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That didn't hurt at all!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.13,0:14:21.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,With this...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.34,0:14:23.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.30,0:14:23.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's doing it again!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.51,0:14:26.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please don't be startled. I'm...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.97,0:14:31.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, I'm...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.97,0:14:32.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the latest model of armor.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.14,0:14:35.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're popular now in Central. Talking armor.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.48,0:14:37.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where's your switch?! Be quiet!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.69,0:14:39.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, you can't turn me off.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.90,0:14:44.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just keep quiet, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.86,0:14:49.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, where are we going?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.33,0:14:50.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To a fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.95,0:14:51.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A fight?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.75,0:14:59.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Boss Poe said that \Nif I wanted to be like him,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.79,0:14:59.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I should go rub out a guy or two.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.46,0:15:02.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So I told him that I would go\Nlay into the Damousha family,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.38,0:15:05.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,who are always\Ninvading our territory.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.38,0:15:08.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I bring back one of\Ntheir heads like this,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.26,0:15:11.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,then no one will treat me like a kid anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.39,0:15:14.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll be accepted as the boss's right-hand-man!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.60,0:15:16.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll do it! I'll flatten them!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.73,0:15:20.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not, by any chance, going to go kill someone?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.11,0:15:28.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're some pretty good armor.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.62,0:15:32.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't even have to worry if they pull a gun on me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.74,0:15:34.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why you're wearing me?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.70,0:15:36.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So it won't hurt?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.29,0:15:37.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.25,0:15:39.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As long as I'm not hurt, I can go all-out.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.84,0:15:42.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's still going to hurt.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.92,0:15:45.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What? Are you a defective product?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.88,0:15:47.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sure it will hurt.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.59,0:15:48.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In your heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.55,0:15:52.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't be silly.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.81,0:15:55.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or would you rather you didn't feel pain in your heart?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.02,0:15:57.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Relax your arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.64,0:15:59.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wh-What is this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.61,0:16:10.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am the Cursed Farmer...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.61,0:16:11.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fscx75\fscy75\pos(355.5,470)}Nyoroi no Noroi
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.82,0:16:11.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I mean,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.28,0:16:15.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the Cursed Armor.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.28,0:16:15.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fscx75\fscy75\pos(380,470)}Noroi no Yoroi
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.45,0:16:20.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once you become one with me,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.45,0:16:23.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,your mind and body will never \Nfeel pain again, forever and ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.55,0:16:26.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.71,0:16:30.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Having been made to live alone together with an old man,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.18,0:16:34.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,she was thinking of what was best for the future, in her own way.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.93,0:16:38.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So she was just hoping to make things easier for her grandpa, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.14,0:16:41.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You did pretty well\Nto have noticed this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.40,0:16:44.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't give you this,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.65,0:16:47.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but if you want, I could introduce you\Nto the engineer who made it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.65,0:16:51.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's got a sharp tongue\Nbut decent skills.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.74,0:16:55.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I appreciate the offer,\Nbut I don't need an artificial leg.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.41,0:16:58.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once you get used to it,\Nit's pretty handy.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.83,0:17:01.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Perhaps so. However...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.92,0:17:06.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, I'd like to leave my leg the way it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.59,0:17:17.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A sword wound I received on\Nthe battlefield became infected.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.89,0:17:21.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By the time they carried me to the rear, all they could do was cut it off.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.31,0:17:24.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Battlefield... You were a soldier?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.15,0:17:26.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Which war?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.90,0:17:29.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The one up north?\NOr...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.61,0:17:31.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't mean Ishbal?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.87,0:17:37.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,On the battlefield,\Neveryone becomes some other creature.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.37,0:17:41.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can carry out even the most cruel acts without any feeling.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.79,0:17:47.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to protect myself, my mind must have shut out all emotions.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.96,0:17:52.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But once the war is over,\Nyou can't keep doing that.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.97,0:17:55.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I must not forget what I saw there...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.76,0:17:58.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,what I did there.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.14,0:18:02.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When I look at this injury, it allows me to remember it all immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.64,0:18:04.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And that's why...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.15,0:18:07.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why you don't want\Nany Automail?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.57,0:18:08.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That isn't very—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.48,0:18:10.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not the only reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.03,0:18:14.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I lost my leg.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.41,0:18:19.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, I have gained something even more important.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.16,0:18:22.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Peace of mind, and a life with my grandchildren.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.75,0:18:24.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You see...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.21,0:18:32.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's once a person loses something\Nthat they first gain something, is it not?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.26,0:18:33.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You think so?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.93,0:18:36.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are those who've\Ngone to war and come back fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.51,0:18:37.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what soldiers do.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.64,0:18:41.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those people have lost something.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.77,0:18:45.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if it isn't something\Nvisible to the eye.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.19,0:18:52.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you've lost something yourself,\Nthen you should've gained something as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.82,0:18:57.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In alchemy, that is what's known as equivalent exchange, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.50,0:19:04.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can that be?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.79,0:19:10.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I lost my right arm and left leg...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.13,0:19:13.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and my brother lost his whole body.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.38,0:19:18.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're living desperately just to get them back!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.76,0:19:19.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Taking everything back—
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.01,0:19:22.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that's what our dream is!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.97,0:19:26.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There isn't a thing\Nwe've gained in return!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.85,0:19:28.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Everything...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.81,0:19:30.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,has been taken from us!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.41,0:19:40.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A dream to take everything back...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.16,0:19:42.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then, once that comes true,\Nwhat will you do?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.79,0:19:48.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A dream that is granted can't be called a real dream at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.90,0:20:12.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even so...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.86,0:20:16.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even so, we're going to take it back.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.49,0:20:20.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks for the tea.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.89,0:20:47.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.48,0:20:50.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Grandpa, Brother is home!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.23,0:20:52.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, that's right! Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.90,0:20:53.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.98,0:20:55.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.65,0:20:58.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.87,0:21:06.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al,\Nyou reek of sheep.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.66,0:21:12.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, excuse me! Fine, when we get to \NGrandma Pinako's house, I'll get washed up.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.42,0:21:14.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Say, Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.34,0:21:18.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Four years ago, when the Colonel came to Resembool,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.84,0:21:22.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he said it was because he happened to look at the letter we sent out, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.93,0:21:24.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what he said.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.85,0:21:26.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He was searching for Dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.14,0:21:32.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But, by any chance, do you think the reason\Nthat the Colonel went to Granny's house was...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.73,0:21:36.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.61,0:21:38.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was worried about you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.07,0:21:40.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.86,0:21:42.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.41,0:21:45.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.83,0:21:50.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry about earlier...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.88,0:21:56.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.09,0:22:01.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we miss this one, we'll have to wait until tomorrow at noon!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.30,0:22:01.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,H-Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.80,0:22:03.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.32,0:22:03.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're going to run!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.93,0:22:06.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the method of\Nshort-distance sprinting
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.93,0:22:08.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that has been passed down \Nthrough my family for generations!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.80,0:22:11.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to break!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.80,0:22:11.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Put me down!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.02,0:23:40.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.77,0:23:44.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 17: "House of the Waiting Family"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.15,0:23:47.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,On the day we left,\Nwe burned down our house.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.07,0:23:50.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We had nowhere to return home to.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.70,0:23:52.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or so we thought...
